LF = ("大家好，我叫陆凡，二零零四年出生，所以是标准的零零后。现在大家都说我们是幸福的一代人，因为我们的父母和许多前辈们给我们创造了非常好的生活和学习条件。我觉得这样说，没错。可是呢，我们这些零零后除了享受这些好条件以外，我们也有很多自己的想法和目标，另外我们跟父母这一辈人的兴趣和爱好也有很大的不同。首先，我们成长的时期是中国的经济和互联网快速发展的时期。从小我们就开始接触和使用互联网和手机。现在网上有很多网络流行语，特别受我们这些零零后的喜爱，因为这样的语言给人的感觉更加可爱，我们不太喜欢过于正式地讲话。同样，我们对世界的看法也有很多是来自于互联网上的信息和各种知识。只要我们想学习，可以每天二十四小时不停地在手机上和网上了解想要知道的信息。正是这个原因，我们的视野更加全球化，目标也更高。比如说，我们这一代人很关心环保，关心地球。我们喜欢骑共享单车，目标就是为了有一个更加绿色的世界。还有，我们的兴趣爱好既广泛，又特别。我们喜欢明星、游戏、交友、自拍、动漫等等。平时我们的学习很紧张，还要上很多的培训班和兴趣班，但这些并没有影响我们成为“动漫迷”。丰富的知识、广阔的视野和众多的兴趣和爱好，让我们这些零零后更加自信。",
      "Activity 4D, script of Lu Fan’s talk (translations mine): Hello everyone, my name is Lu Fan. I was born in 2004, so I am a typical post-2000s kid. Now everyone says we are a happy generation, because our parents and many elders created very good living and study conditions for us. I think that’s right. But besides enjoying these good conditions, we post-2000s also have many ideas and goals of our own, and our interests and hobbies differ greatly from our parents’ generation. First, the period in which we grew up was one of rapid development of China’s economy and the internet. From childhood we began to come into contact with and use the internet and phones. There are now many internet slang words, especially loved by us post-2000s, because such language feels cuter and we don’t like to speak too formally. Likewise, many of our views of the world come from information and knowledge on the internet. As long as we want to learn, we can find out the information we want on phones and online 24 hours a day without stopping. It is precisely for this reason that our horizons are more global and our goals higher. For example, our generation cares a lot about environmental protection and the earth. We like to ride shared bikes, with the aim of a greener world. Also, our interests and hobbies are both broad and special. We like celebrities, games, making friends, selfies, anime and so on. Our studies are usually tense and we also attend many training classes and interest classes, but these haven’t stopped us from becoming “anime fans.” Rich knowledge, broad horizons and many interests and hobbies make us post-2000s even more confident. (the book writes 2004, 00 后 and 24 with digits)")
QA4 = table(["Question", "My answer (the book gives none)"], [["B1. Who is the speaker?", "Lu Fan, a student born in 2004, one of the post-2000s generation"], ["B2. How many different attributes of the speaker’s generation are described? What are they?", "Four: they grew up with the internet and phones (and love net slang); their views of the world come from the internet, giving global horizons and higher goals such as caring about the environment; their interests are broad and special (celebrities, games, friends, selfies, anime); and rich knowledge, vision and interests make them more confident"], ["B3. What is your impression of the speaker?", "Confident, thoughtful and cheerful"], ["C1. What is the general view of the speaker’s generation?", "That they are a happy generation, since parents and elders created very good living and study conditions"], ["C2. Does the speaker agree? What is the speaker’s argument?", "Agrees (“没错”), but adds that they also have their own ideas and goals, and interests different from their parents’"], ["C3. The impact of the internet and mobile devices", "Contact with the internet and phones from childhood; popular net slang; learning information 24 hours a day; a more global outlook and higher goals"], ["C4. Hobbies and interests", "Celebrities, games, making friends, selfies, anime"], ["C5. What contributes to the speaker’s confidence?", "Rich knowledge, broad horizons and many interests and hobbies"], ["E. Characteristics of Generation Z in the U.S.", "(left to the learners)"]], title="Skill Integration Review, Activity 4: questions and my answers")
IP1 = dlg([
    ("主持人", "大家好，欢迎大家来参加我们的节目。今天我们非常高兴地请到了两位教育方面的专家：一位是来自北京大学的王林教授；另一位呢是人民大学的张刚教授。", "Part 1 script (translations mine). Host: Hello everyone, welcome to our program. Today we are delighted to have two experts in education: Professor Wang Lin from Peking University and Professor Zhang Gang from Renmin University."),
    ("王林", "大家好！", "Wang Lin: Hello everyone!"),
    ("张刚", "大家好！", "Zhang Gang: Hello everyone!"),
    ("主持人", "你们二位都是教育专家，请先说说我们国家留守儿童和流动儿童的情况，好吗？", "Host: You are both education experts; please first tell us about the situation of left-behind children and migrant children in our country, all right?"),
    ("王林", "好的。我们大家都知道，现在中国的农村呢有大量的留守儿童，主要就是那些父母需要到城市里打工而被留在老家跟自己的爷爷、奶奶、外公、外婆或亲戚一起生活的孩子们。他们常常很久见不到自己父母。", "Wang Lin: All right. We all know that rural China now has a great many left-behind children, mainly children whose parents have to go work in cities and who are left in their hometowns to live with their grandparents or relatives. They often can’t see their parents for a long time."),
    ("主持人", "那打工的父母为什么不把孩子也带到城市里呢？", "Host: Then why don’t the working parents bring their children to the city?"),
    ("王林", "一般来说，打工的父母们工作非常辛苦，每天要工作很长时间，他们没有时间来照顾自己的孩子。还有一个原因就是，城市里的生活很贵，有些父母没有足够的钱可以让自己的孩子们在城里生活。", "Wang Lin: Generally, working parents work very hard, long hours every day, and have no time to look after their children. Another reason is that life in the city is expensive, and some parents don’t have enough money for their children to live in the city."),
    ("主持人", "这些留守儿童们在农村都是怎么生活的呢？", "Host: How do these left-behind children live in the countryside?"),
    ("王林", "他们主要是由家里年纪比较大的老人们来照顾，给他们做饭、送他们去上学等等。但是，孩子们很少有父母的关爱，也很少有机会跟父母交流。", "Wang Lin: They are mainly looked after by the older people at home, who cook for them, take them to school and so on. But the children rarely have their parents’ love and care, and rarely have a chance to talk with their parents."),
])
IP2 = dlg([
    ("主持人", "那流动儿童又是什么样的孩子呢？张教授，请你来谈谈，好吗？", "Part 2 script. Host: And what kind of children are migrant children? Professor Zhang, please tell us, will you?"),
    ("张刚", "好的。现在我们所说的“流动儿童”就是指那些随着打工的父母到城市里生活至少半年以上的孩子们。跟留守儿童相比，他们更幸运一些，至少能够和自己的父母在一起，能得到父母的照顾和爱护。", "Zhang Gang: All right. What we now call “migrant children” are children who follow their working parents to live in the city for at least half a year. Compared with left-behind children they are somewhat luckier: at least they can be with their parents and get their care and love."),
    ("主持人", "为什么我们不可以让更多的留守儿童变成流动儿童呢？", "Host: Why can’t we let more left-behind children become migrant children?"),
    ("张刚", "虽然流动儿童的生活和环境好一些，但是他们同样也有很多的困难。比如上学的问题。开始的时候，流动儿童进入城市里的公立学校需要交很多的钱。", "Zhang Gang: Although migrant children’s life and environment are somewhat better, they too have many difficulties, for example school. At the start, migrant children had to pay a lot of money to enter public schools in the city."),
    ("主持人", "那现在呢？", "Host: And now?"),
    ("张刚", "现在百分之八十的孩子可以去附近的公办学校读书。另外的百分之二十可能会去一些打工子弟的学校，但这些学校的教育质量比较差，甚至有的还不如农村的学校。", "Zhang Gang: Now 80 percent of the children can go to a nearby public school. The other 20 percent may go to some migrant workers’ children’s schools, but the education quality at these schools is relatively poor, and some are even not as good as rural schools. (the book writes 80% and 20% in digits)"),
    ("主持人", "所以，总的来说流动儿童的条件比以前好一些。", "Host: So, on the whole, migrant children’s conditions are somewhat better than before."),
    ("张刚", "是这样的。不过，因为打工的父母常常换工作，或者搬到别的城市去打工，这些流动儿童不得不跟着父母不停地搬家，进入一个新的学校，习惯一个新的环境。这样，对孩子也会有很大的影响。", "Zhang Gang: That’s right. But because working parents often change jobs or move to other cities to work, these migrant children have no choice but to keep moving with their parents, entering a new school and getting used to a new environment. This too has a great impact on the children."),
    ("主持人", "好的，现在我们休息一下。待会儿接着再聊。", "Host: All right, let’s take a break now and continue chatting later. (the book prints 呆会儿, read here as 待会儿)"),
])
Q5 = [("美国有留守儿童或流动儿童吗？", "Activity 5E (translations mine): Are there left-behind or migrant children in America?"), ("如果有，请描述一下他们的生活。", "If so, please describe their life."), ("如果没有，请解释为什么没有这样的情况？", "If not, please explain why there is no such situation?")]
QA5 = table(["Question", "My answer (the book gives none)"], [["A1. What is the topic of the interview?", "留守儿童和流动儿童 (left-behind children and migrant children)"], ["A2. Who are the two guest speakers?", "Two professors, one from Beijing University and one from Renmin University"], ["B Part 1, 1. The guest’s definition of the children’s group", "Children left in their hometown with grandparents or relatives because their parents work in cities"], ["B Part 1, 2. Why have these children been left behind?", "The parents work long hours with no time for them, and city life is expensive"], ["B Part 1, 3. How do they live? Three details", "Looked after by older people; cooked for and taken to school; seldom have parental love or chances to talk with parents"], ["B Part 2, 1. The definition of the group", "Children who follow working parents to live in the city for at least half a year"], ["B Part 2, 2. Are they more fortunate? Why?", "Yes, somewhat: they can be with their parents and get their care and love"], ["B Part 2, 3. Difficulties, three details", "School fees and entering schools; some schools have poor quality; frequent moves to new schools and environments"]], title="Skill Integration Review, Activity 5: the interview, questions and my answers")
L3 = lesson(
    "Lesson 30 Skill Integration Review: a post-2000s speaker and a TV interview on left-behind and migrant children",
    "陆凡 · 零零后 · 幸福的一代人 · 视野 · 动漫迷 · 自信 · 留守儿童和流动儿童 · 公办学校 · 打工子弟学校",
    requires=[],
    cards=[
        card("Skill Integration Review, Activity 4 (Listening, Reading, Writing, and Speaking)", "A. Pre-listening: Guess the meaning of the following words. If necessary, look them up in your dictionary. Predict what you will hear and share your answers with a classmate. B. Listen to the passage and answer the following questions: 1. Who is the speaker? 2. How many different attributes of the speaker’s generation are described? And what are they? 3. What is your impression of the speaker? C. Listen to the passage a second time and write detailed information for the following questions: 1. What is the general view of the speaker’s generation? 2. Does the speaker agree or not? What is the speaker’s argument? 3. List the impact of the internet and mobile devices on the speaker’s generation. 4. List the hobbies and interests of the speaker’s generation. 5. What contributes to the speaker’s confidence? D. Work in groups of three and share your answers with your partners. Read the script and check whether you have additional questions. E. In the same group, discuss the characteristics of Generation Z in the U.S. The words, the script and my answers:", tables=[SUP, QA4], examples=[D(*LF)]),
        card("Skill Integration Review, Activity 5 (Listening, Reading, Writing, and Speaking)", "Listen to a TV interview about children from the countryside and complete the tasks. A. Listen to the interview once and answer the multiple-choice questions: 1. What is the topic of the interview? (农村的留守儿童 / 城市里的流动儿童 / 留守儿童和流动儿童 / 留守儿童的心理问题) 2. Who are the two guest speakers? (Two journalists / Two experts from the Ministry of Education / Two professors, one from Beijing University and one from Qinghua University / Two professors, one from Beijing University and one from Renmin University) B. Pair up. Each partner listens to one part of the interview and answers the related questions. C. When you have answered the questions, exchange information with your partner and ask each other the questions. Write down their answers. D. Read the scripts together and check your information. E. Work in groups of three and discuss the following questions. The scripts and my answers:", tables=[QA5], examples=IP1 + IP2 + [D(z, e) for z, e in Q5]),
    ],
    exercises=[
        M("When was Lu Fan born?", "2004", ["1994", "1984", "2014"], "二零零四年出生."),
        M("Why do people call Lu Fan’s generation happy?", "Parents and elders created very good living and study conditions", ["They are rich", "They have no exams", "They have no parents"], "我们的父母和许多前辈们给我们创造了非常好的生活和学习条件."),
        M("What kind of language do the post-2000s like?", "Cute internet slang rather than overly formal speech", ["Only classical Chinese", "Only English", "Only formal speech"], "我们不太喜欢过于正式地讲话."),
        M("What do the post-2000s care about, per Lu Fan?", "Environmental protection and the earth", ["Only fashion", "Only money", "Only sports"], "很关心环保，关心地球."),
        M("What do they like, besides games and celebrities?", "Making friends, selfies, anime", ["Gardening", "Cooking", "Knitting"], "交友、自拍、动漫."),
        M("What makes Lu Fan’s generation more confident?", "Rich knowledge, broad horizons and many interests", ["Money", "Fame", "Age"], "丰富的知识、广阔的视野和众多的兴趣和爱好."),
        M("Who are the two guests in the TV interview?", "Two education professors", ["Two journalists", "Two ministers", "Two students"], "两位教育方面的专家."),
        M("Why don’t working parents bring their children to the city?", "No time to look after them, and city life is expensive", ["The children refuse", "No schools exist", "It is illegal"], "没有时间来照顾自己的孩子……城市里的生活很贵."),
        M("How long must a child live in the city to count as a “migrant child”?", "At least half a year", ["At least a week", "At least five years", "A day"], "至少半年以上."),
        M("What share of migrant children can now attend nearby public schools?", "80 percent", ["8 percent", "18 percent", "100 percent"], "现在百分之八十的孩子可以去附近的公办学校读书."),
        M("What is another difficulty for migrant children?", "Frequent moves to new schools and environments", ["Too many holidays", "No friends at all", "Free tuition"], "不停地搬家，进入一个新的学校，习惯一个新的环境."),
        F("我们的视野更加全球___，目标也更高。", "化", ["式", "的", "性"], "全球化: globalized."),
        F("这些学校的教育质量比较差，甚至有的还不如农村的学___。", "校", ["习", "生", "堂"], "学校: school."),
    ],
)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ 4. act 6
NA = [("随着科技和人工智能的发展，智能手机和手机应用越来越普遍，特别是在中国。如果你是最近到中国旅游过的外国人，你会发现当代的中国人长途旅行坐高铁，市内交通打滴滴，购物上淘宝，吃饭叫美团、饿了么，聊天付款靠微信，一切尽在掌上——一个智能手机就能走遍天下。", "Activity 6, paragraph 1 (translations mine): With the development of technology and artificial intelligence, smartphones and phone apps are becoming more and more common, especially in China. If you are a foreigner who has recently traveled in China, you will find that today’s Chinese take high-speed rail for long trips, use DiDi in the city, shop on Taobao, order meals from Meituan and Ele.me, and chat and pay with WeChat; everything is in the palm of your hand, and one smartphone can take you everywhere."),
      ("在上海工作的美国人珍妮，已经习惯了这样的生活方式。她最经常使用的一款外卖软件叫“美团”。她也尝试下载使用过其他的外卖软件，比如“饿了么”，但用得最多的还是“美团”。现在珍妮已经成了外卖点餐的大户，她每天要在外卖平台上点两顿餐，甚至有时候会点第三顿。首先，因为她喜欢中国菜，什么菜都想试吃一下。另外，她喜欢根据外卖平台上的图片点外卖，所以每次点外卖的时候都很开心。虽然她看不懂外卖软件上餐厅的中文介绍和用户评价，但是只要看到照片她就会很惊喜。能够在一个平台上点那么多餐厅的饭菜，而且还有电子发票和账单，扫一下“二维码”就可以手机付款，对她来说，这简直太幸福了。", "Paragraph 2: Jenny, an American working in Shanghai, is already used to this way of life. The takeout app she uses most is called “Meituan.” She has also tried downloading other takeout apps, such as “Ele.me,” but the one she uses most is still “Meituan.” Jenny has now become a heavy takeout customer: she orders two meals a day on the platform and sometimes even a third. First, because she likes Chinese food and wants to try every dish. Also, she likes ordering according to the pictures on the platform, so she is happy every time. Although she can’t read the restaurants’ Chinese descriptions and user reviews on the app, as long as she sees the photos she is pleasantly surprised. Being able to order from so many restaurants on one platform, with electronic invoices and bills, and paying by phone by scanning a “QR code,” is simply too happy a thing for her."),
      ("来自荷兰的玛丽说，到中国之后她发现使用手机的机会特别多，比如说：打车软件、共享单车小程序等。很多外国人在中国生活的时候发现在这里的打车软件特别流行和受欢迎，似乎每个人都会用打车软件，不光叫快车、专车，还能招到出租车。第一次去中国，那儿的朋友告诉她必须下载两个手机应用：一个是微信；另一个就是滴滴。有了它们，她可以去中国的任何一个地方。如果手机上没有滴滴出行，她就寸步难行。玛丽很少打车，只有当她要去一趟北京特别远的郊区，她才会使用网约车。相对来说，她更喜欢尝试共享单车。在荷兰，大部分人都喜欢骑自行车出行。", "Paragraph 3: Mary, from the Netherlands, says that after arriving in China she found there were especially many chances to use the phone, for example ride-hailing apps and shared-bike mini programs. Many foreigners living in China find that ride-hailing apps are especially popular here; it seems everyone uses them, not only to call express and private cars but even to hail taxis. On her first trip to China, friends there told her she must download two apps: one was WeChat and the other DiDi. With them she can go anywhere in China. Without DiDi on her phone she could hardly take a step. Mary rarely takes a car; only when she has to go to a particularly far suburb of Beijing does she use a ride-hailing car. Relatively speaking she prefers trying shared bikes. In the Netherlands most people like to travel by bike."),
      ("其实除了聊天、移动支付、叫外卖、打车之外，在中国也有很多人在手机上安装民宿、短租平台的应用软件，实现“一键”式的民宿短租预定，真正实现了“衣食住行”都在手机上。来自加拿大的留学生杰西说，中国人每天好像就住在自己的手机里。说到旅行住宿，他发现很多中国的年轻人现在都喜欢住民宿、短租房。他的很多中国朋友喜欢用中国本土的小猪短租、蚂蚁短租等平台。但是，对他来说，“爱彼迎”的英文平台更方便一些。不过，有时候跟中国朋友一起旅行，他也跟他们一样，通过中文的短租平台，找到一些非常便宜的民宿。他特别喜欢那些有中国文化特色和当地习俗的民宿。有些房主还亲自给房客做家常菜和当地的饭，这让杰西觉得可以有更多美好的回忆。他也喜欢通过手机应用给房主打分，写评价。还有，他也经常在旅行中给自己的家人发送照片，分享在中国的经历。", "Paragraph 4: In fact, besides chatting, mobile payment, ordering takeout and hailing rides, many people in China also install homestay and short-term-rental apps on their phones, making “one-key” bookings possible, truly realizing “clothing, food, housing and transport” all on the phone. Jesse, an international student from Canada, says that Chinese people seem to live in their phones every day. Speaking of travel lodging, he found that many young Chinese now like homestays and short-term rentals. Many of his Chinese friends like using Chinese platforms such as Xiaozhu Duanzu and Mayi Duanzu. But for him, the English platform of “Airbnb” is a bit more convenient. Still, when traveling with Chinese friends he too, like them, finds some very cheap homestays through the Chinese platforms. He especially likes homestays with Chinese cultural features and local customs. Some hosts even personally cook home-style and local dishes for guests, which lets Jesse feel he has more beautiful memories. He also likes rating hosts and writing reviews through the phone app. Also, he often sends photos to his family during travel, sharing his experiences in China.")]
TT6 = table(["Activity 6", "Task (the article is printed twice in the book; the tables are blank and the book gives no key)"], [["A", "Pair up and read the first paragraph together. Share your understanding of the paragraph and predict what information you can expect in the paragraphs that follow. (Your Prediction:)"], ["B", "Work in groups of three. Each group member reads one paragraph of the following article. Summarize your paragraph and complete the details in the table, then share your information with your partners and take notes on their information. Student 1, Paragraph 2: Main idea of the paragraph; Who; What platform & app used; What the person does with the app; Reasons for using the app; Other information. Student 2, Paragraph 3: Main idea; Who; What platform & app used; Services provided by the app; Reasons for using the app; What the person does with the app. Student 3, Paragraph 4: Main idea; Who; What platform & app used; What the person does with the app; Reasons for using the app; Other information."], ["C", "Quickly read through the other two paragraphs not assigned to you. Then tell your partners what you would do in China if you were working or studying there today."]], title="Skill Integration Review, Activity 6 (Reading, Writing, and Speaking): the tasks")
